    <section class=3D"copy-section" aria-labelledby=3D"insights-heading">
      <h2 id=3D"insights-heading" class=3D"section-title">Insights</h2>
      <p class=3D"calc-note">Generated from the current filter set. These a=
re observations from the 24-row file, not forecasts.</p>
      <ul id=3D"insights-list" class=3D"insight-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Nairobi leads revenue</h3>
        <p>Nairobi accounts for KES 612,000 (39.28%) of recognised revenue =
in this view, from 8 completed orders.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Nakuru is the smallest completed book</h3>
        <p>Nakuru contributed KES 260,000 (16.69%) and 4 completed orders. =
AOV here is KES 65,000.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>March is the peak; February is the trough</h3>
        <p>March 2026 is the strongest month (KES 614,000). February 2026 i=
s the weakest (KES 460,000). February is -4.96% versus January. March is 33=
.48% versus February.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Electronics carry sales; furniture carries margin</h3>
        <p>Electronics are KES 1,110,000 (71.25%) at 28.83% margin. Furnitu=
re is KES 448,000 at 38.84% margin.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Laptop leads revenue; Office Chair leads units</h3>
        <p>Laptop generated KES 525,000. Office Chair sold 14 units. Laptop=
 has the thinnest completed margin in this view (26.67%).</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Returns in this view are phones</h3>
        <p>2 of 6 phone orders were returned (33.33%). Returned IDs: 1006, =
1022. Non-phone returns: none in this filter.</p>
      </li></ul>
    </section>

    <section class=3D"copy-section" aria-labelledby=3D"rec-heading">
      <h2 id=3D"rec-heading" class=3D"section-title">Recommendations</h2>
      <p class=3D"calc-note">Fixed to the full Q1 file so they do not drift=
 when filters change. Each item cites a finding.</p>
      <ol class=3D"rec-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Review phone quality in Nairobi and Kisumu</h3>
          <p><strong>Finding.</strong> Orders 1006 and 1022 are the only re=
turns. Both are phones sold to returning customers =E2=80=94 2 of 6 phone o=
rders (33%). Reversed list value is KES 90,000.</p>
          <p><strong>Do.</strong> Inspect phone fulfilment and after-sales =
in those two cities and start recording return reasons. The rest of the ran=
ge had 0 of 18 orders returned.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Recover Nakuru=E2=80=99s cancelled tablet and list chairs</h3=
>
          <p><strong>Finding.</strong> Nakuru is last on revenue (KES 260,0=
00, 16.69%) and AOV (KES 65,000). Order 1014 cancelled KES 50,000 of tablet=
s. No completed tablets and no office chairs in Nakuru.</p>
          <p><strong>Do.</strong> Follow up that February cancellation and =
trial office chairs, the highest-margin SKU (41.67%) elsewhere.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Attach furniture to lift blended margin</h3>
          <p><strong>Finding.</strong> Furniture margin is 38.84% versus 28=
.83% on electronics. Chairs lead units (14) and unit margin, but are only 1=
0.78% of revenue.</p>
          <p><strong>Do.</strong> Bundle desk + chair in cities that alread=
y sell both. Keep electronics listed; this is mix, not a category exit.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Treat laptops as a margin project, not a volume cut</h3>
          <p><strong>Finding.</strong> Laptops are 33.70% of revenue (KES 5=
25,000) at the thinnest unit margin (26.67%). February=E2=80=99s revenue di=
p tracks laptop units falling from 3 to 1.</p>
          <p><strong>Do.</strong> Work unit cost and attach a chair or desk=
 on laptop tickets. Keep stock: March recovered when laptop units returned =
to 3.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Copy Mombasa completion and staff a March-like mix</h3>
          <p><strong>Finding.</strong> Mombasa completed 5 of 5 orders acro=
ss all five SKUs. March revenue rose 33.48% to KES 614,000; laptops plus de=
sks were KES 400,000 of that month.</p>
          <p><strong>Do.</strong> Standardise Mombasa=E2=80=99s pick-and-co=
nfirm steps in the cities that returned or cancelled, and align inventory t=
o laptops and desks for high-volume weeks.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

